Build zip with deflate only. EPUB containers hold stored and deflated
entries, and the zip crate's default features add bzip2, LZMA, XZ, PPMd,
Zstandard, Deflate64, AES and a second deflate backend: about 0.9 MB of a
static ARM binary for codecs no EPUB uses. flate2 keeps its default
(miniz_oxide) backend.

--- a/crates/core/Cargo.toml
+++ b/crates/core/Cargo.toml
@@ -19,7 +19,7 @@
 titlecase = "3.6.0"
 unicode-normalization = "0.1.25"
 toml = "0.9.11"
-zip = "7.0.0"
+zip = { version = "7.0.0", default-features = false, features = ["deflate-flate2"] }
 kl-hyphenate = "0.7.3"
 entities = "1.0.1"
 paragraph-breaker = "0.4.4"
